r-right AfD over the past decade has made clear the first argument was wron=
g. The second=3F We=E2=80=99ll see.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/=
25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The AfD won big in a s=
tate election on Sunday. It not only won more than twice as many votes as t=
he nearest contender. It won with the biggest voter turnout since reunifica=
tion. In most circumstances, that would count as a clear mandate to govern.=
 The AfD, though, still might not be able to.</span></p><p style=3D"font:no=
rmal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>For years, G=
ermany=E2=80=99s entire political establishment has made common cause to st=
op the far right from exercising power. Now, a question that has long been =
raised by AfD voters is being debated in mainstream circles, too: Are these=
 efforts to sideline the AfD in the name of democracy actually undermining =
democracy=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;colo=
