heir only common ground=3F Keep out the AfD</span></p><p style=3D"font:norm=
al 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>AfD supporters=
 would say democracy wasn=E2=80=99t working properly to start with. The AfD=
 =E2=80=94 the Alternative for Germany =E2=80=94 was created in 2013, at a =
time when German voters didn=E2=80=99t have much of an alternative. Former =
Chancellor Angela Merkel, on the center-right, made a habit of going into c=
oalition with her party=E2=80=99s traditional opponents on the center-left,=
 which meant, in effect, that whatever party you voted for, you=E2=80=99d g=
et the same government.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia=
,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The AfD thrived in that vacuum.</s=
pan></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0=
 0 15px"><span>And as its vote share has reached new highs =E2=80=94 polls =
show it=E2=80=99s the </span><a href=3D"https://nl.nytimes.com/f/a/uTIIgJPo=
